{"chapter": "morphisms", "node_kind": "section_title", "parent_tag": "01W0", "placeholders": {}, "render": {"prefix": "\\section{", "suffix": "}\n\\label{section-proper}"}, "risk_level": "R1", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:0d026470de8e7141da171856c34384f562a5f75da3a34046a802f5bc367a3370", "source_text": "Proper morphisms", "source_text_hash": "sha256:d19cc9591ee6ed3ebbad959c8358a86e01df1fa59b906de236f42e5ffddbc338", "unit_id": "tag:01W0:title"}
{"chapter": "morphisms", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "01W0", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\mathbf{P}^n_S \\to S$", "MATH_0002": "$n$", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:e1a34fb0a3976640b560f627a7a9a78534d342f2fdb2d151e2d79d14788778e5", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:a118c1a68bbfdb60ad3c48d56626e4b012432dc8f8595897e006477ad18f8083", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nThe notion of a proper morphism plays an important role in algebraic\ngeometry. An important example of a proper morphism will be the\nstructure morphism <MATH_0001> of projective <MATH_0002>-space,\nand this is in fact the motivating example leading to the definition.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:572d6ad8c51659a967e7c1c098df72256ead3254d158bc6d2862e00261a40149", "unit_id": "tag:01W0:prose-0001"}
{"chapter": "morphisms", "node_kind": "definition", "parent_tag": "01W0", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$f : X \\to S$", "MATH_0002": "$f$", "MATH_0003": "$f$", "TEXTITCLOSE_0001": "}", "TEXTITOPEN_0001": "{\\it "}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{definition}\n\\label{definition-proper}\n", "suffix": "\\end{definition}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:91f7f690005974538f9413d26e06567c7aaac53ad99387d497b14ae3e3c887e8", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:c63d04b580ce01c580c79c9f617cde7185ca4de405f0495de672a438468e84f1", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a morphism of schemes.\nWe say <MATH_0002> is <TEXTITOPEN_0001>proper<TEXTITCLOSE_0001> if <MATH_0003> is separated, finite type, and\nuniversally closed.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:0cad03cbdba4cf5c52d532d055addf72405cd9ae31b1f055d1da7dd771049bb1", "unit_id": "tag:01W1:statement"}
{"chapter": "morphisms", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "01W0", "placeholders": {"STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:7c4b7f1483a6f0c8c2a87d2110be465962e13648bb17ef2e915ed0d25f17ba22", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nThe morphism from the affine line with zero doubled to the affine line\nis of finite type and universally closed, so the separation condition is\nnecessary in the definition above.\nIn the rest of this section we prove some of the basic properties\nof proper morphisms and of universally closed morphisms.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:de60229c8c35b719a09882e36b32bbf9d710e60def098ec32e33e6850686e319", "unit_id": "tag:01W0:prose-0002"}
{"chapter": "morphisms", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "01W0", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$f : X \\to S$", "MATH_0002": "$f$", "MATH_0003": "$S = \\bigcup V_j$", "MATH_0004": "$f^{-1}(V_j) \\to V_j$", "MATH_0005": "$j$", "STRUCT_0001": "\\begin{enumerate}", "STRUCT_0002": "\\item", "STRUCT_0003": "\\item", "STRUCT_0004": "\\end{enumerate}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-universally-closed-local-on-the-base}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:e521c3fd474a4d2087f1e8d4a3f3d04657ec90e515b854f939e4482b5cad35c9", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:1664267e8625d9bcc108b588ed94bcb3c8c1996982660659d551223d69026f60", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a morphism of schemes.\nThe following are equivalent:\n<STRUCT_0001>\n<STRUCT_0002> The morphism <MATH_0002> is universally closed.\n<STRUCT_0003> There exists an open covering <MATH_0003> such\nthat <MATH_0004> is universally closed for all indices <MATH_0005>.\n<STRUCT_0004>\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:d84ba53638ed8f57b1d82398cd9afdea614e0d38623e34b12864222fdf81e7c8", "unit_id": "tag:02K7:statement"}
{"chapter": "morphisms", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "01W0", "placeholders": {}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:903c2fdbb2db7728d5f25d68ecc114c25252c70231e64eeead7ca0f28a9e7186", "source_text": "This is clear from the definition.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:f0d180afa3ff52806f2998b6e4edf0d7ba9131e16ce38b5289d490e97da8dd4e", "unit_id": "tag:02K7:proof"}
{"chapter": "morphisms", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "01W0", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$f : X \\to S$", "MATH_0002": "$f$", "MATH_0003": "$S = \\bigcup V_j$", "MATH_0004": "$f^{-1}(V_j) \\to V_j$", "MATH_0005": "$j$", "STRUCT_0001": "\\begin{enumerate}", "STRUCT_0002": "\\item", "STRUCT_0003": "\\item", "STRUCT_0004": "\\end{enumerate}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-proper-local-on-the-base}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:e521c3fd474a4d2087f1e8d4a3f3d04657ec90e515b854f939e4482b5cad35c9", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:dee460be021a3c4be5bfda9e7f57500a1db2487160247e28f3943bcca87480e2", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a morphism of schemes.\nThe following are equivalent:\n<STRUCT_0001>\n<STRUCT_0002> The morphism <MATH_0002> is proper.\n<STRUCT_0003> There exists an open covering <MATH_0003> such\nthat <MATH_0004> is proper for all indices <MATH_0005>.\n<STRUCT_0004>\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:5ff5e0e72c0edde50ec92fc20ac7776d5447515dfc17f5e69566693cd110503c", "unit_id": "tag:01W2:statement"}
